course: dictionary
lesson: 14568
title: Pidgin: a language built to talk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes people who speak different languages need to talk to each other, for example to buy and sell goods. They mix words from both languages into a simple new way of speaking. This is called a pidgin. «The traders in the port used a pidgin of English and their own words to buy and sell goods.» The clues are traders, port and buy and sell, so a pidgin is a simple language for trade.
explain: The second meaning is informal. If someone speaks «pidgin French», their French is broken or very simple, because they do not know it well. «Mum laughed at my pidgin Spanish, but she understood every word.» The clue is that Mum understood, so the speech was rough but still worked.
fact: A pidgin is a simple language that people make up when they need to talk across different languages.
fact: Pidgins often grew up in ports and on plantations, where people from many places met to work and trade.
fact: When children grow up speaking a pidgin as their first language, it becomes a full language called a creole.
fact: Tok Pisin in Papua New Guinea and Nigerian Pidgin are well-known examples, spoken by millions of people.
fact: Informally, «pidgin French» means broken or very simple French from someone who does not know the language well.
exercise: «The sailors and the shopkeepers used a pidgin to trade.» What is a pidgin here? | A type of ship used for fishing | A dictionary of hard words | *A simple language made so people who speak different languages can talk | A kind of market stall
exercise: «She spoke pidgin Spanish on holiday, mixing in a few words of her own.» What does pidgin suggest about her Spanish? | Written in capital letters | *Broken and very simple, not fully correct | Spoken only by old people | Perfect and very fluent
exercise: Jordan says, «Tok Pisin is just broken English.» What is the right answer? | Tok Pisin is spoken by only one family | Tok Pisin is a single word | Tok Pisin is a type of fish | *Tok Pisin is a full language, used by millions, with its own rules
test: What does a pidgin become when children grow up speaking it as their first language? | *A creole, which is a full language | A dictionary | A port | Nothing, it stays broken
test: Where did pidgins often grow up, according to the lesson? | *In ports and on plantations, where people from many places met | Inside castles on hills | On the moon | Only in schools
exam: Which best describes a pidgin? | *A simple language made up so people who speak different languages can talk | A broken word in English only | A kind of drum | A type of plant
